From ea5accd39c67725628a86f3979f8153743f29d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:20:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: make the tab sheet close morph travel into the real
 bar's icon size and text origin

In the frames before the close hand-off the pill's icon copies were drawn
about 1.4x larger than the real toolbar icons and dropped to the real size
in one frame when the hand-off started. The url text also jumped 4 to 10 px
on that frame and then settled.

The icon copy before the hand-off was the real icon's drawable, scaled to
the whole padded box of the view. The real view draws it inside its padding,
so the glyph filled the box and was larger than the real one. The hand-off
copies a bitmap of the real view (its padding, scale type and badge), which
is why the size dropped on that frame. The url text jumped for two reasons.
The pill took the real url view's own left and right inset as its text inset
once the sheet had moved, but the glyphs sit further in by the view's
padding, so the text and the point it ellipsizes at were off by that padding.
And the first glyph and the baseline were aligned to the real ones only from
the hand-off on.

While the sheet travels toward closed, the icon copies are now bitmaps of
the real icon views, the same as in the hand-off. The pill's text inset
keeps the stored resting glyph inset the whole way down instead of only on
the first frame. The pill's text views are shifted by the gap between the
real first glyph and baseline, as they sit in the real bar, and the pill's
own, as they sit in the pill, weighted by one less the morph's ease. The
shift is the whole alignment the hand-off makes when the pill is on the bar
rect and nothing where the pill has become the small pill, so the first
hand-off frame moves nothing. The direction comes from the last frame that
moved the sheet (a close, a drag down or a pull back down), so the way up
keeps the drawable copies, the pill's own inset and no shift. A reopen, a
drag that turns back up and a teardown clear the shift.

The 130 ms fade, the url bitmap, the circular favicon copy, the bar band,
the plus highlight, the page and top toolbar restore and the open path are
unchanged. The unit tests cover the icon copy's bitmap, size and place
across the hand-off frame, the drawable copy on the way up, the text's
first glyph, baseline, width and inset before and across the hand-off, the
shift fading out with the morph, and its removal on a turn back up and on a
reopen.
---
